        <detaileddescription>
<para>The averaged current is <computeroutput>4000 mA x I_AVG_MANT / TP_MANT</computeroutput>, so TP_MANT is the divisor <emphasis>and</emphasis> sets the resolution: 4000/TP_MANT mA per I_AVG_MANT count. At 64 counts that is ~62 mA/count, already coarse; below it a single count of noise swings the result by hundreds of mA. TP_MANT lands in that range only when the measurement window never ran (<ref refid="namespacetle92466ed_1_1DITHER__CLK__DIV" kindref="compound">DITHER_CLK_DIV</ref> at its POR value of 0, or feedback frozen by FB_FRZ) or when the reply frame was spliced on a shared bus — never during healthy operation. </para>
